{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Take a goat.</b> Let a goat come and atone for the deed of Joseph's goat. Another interpretation: <b>Take a goat</b> to atone for idolatry that they committed, for we find that goats are burned — these are the goats of idolatry that are burned outside the camp, as stated in the Tanchuma — and this one is burned."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:48.791829759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}